<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Core Mechanisms, Efficiency, and Parameter Configuration of MAT-Agent</h2>

<div id="Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This supplementary material aims to provide a more detailed and in-depth explanation of the MAT-Agent framework, addressing key questions and concerns raised during the review process regarding its agent coordination mechanisms, computational efficiency considerations, state and action space design, and hyperparameter configurations. We hope these clarifications will resolve related doubts and comprehensively demonstrate the completeness and rigor of this research work.</p>
</div>
<section id="Ax1.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">S 1.1 Detailed Explanation of Agent Coordination Mechanism</h3>

<div id="Ax1.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multiple autonomous agents within the MAT-Agent framework achieve efficient collaboration to optimize the training process of multi-label image classification (MLIC) through the following interconnected core mechanisms:</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.SSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="Ax1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Ax1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shared Global State Representation (<math id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> All agents, at each decision step <math id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, access and utilize a comprehensive, real-time updated extended state representation <math id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The state <math id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is carefully designed to integrate the MLIC model’s immediate learning performance metrics (<math id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}^{perf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}^{perf}</annotation></semantics></math>), complex dynamic characteristics of the training process (<math id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}^{dyn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}^{dyn}</annotation></semantics></math>), and descriptors reflecting current data characteristics (<math id="Ax1.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}^{data}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}^{data}</annotation></semantics></math>). This global information sharing ensures that all agents make decisions based on a unified understanding of the current training environment, forming the foundation for their effective coordinated actions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unified Global Composite Reward Signal (<math id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> After all agents collectively determine and execute a joint training configuration <math id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}=(a_{t}^{AUG},a_{t}^{OPT},a_{t}^{LRS},a_{t}^{LOSS})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}=(a_{t}^{AUG},a_{t}^{OPT},a_{t}^{LRS},a_{t}^{LOSS})</annotation></semantics></math>, the system computes a scalar reward signal <math id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> based on the overall performance of this configuration (rather than the isolated effect of individual agent actions), which is then shared among all agents. The reward function</p>
<table id="Ax1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}=w_{mAP}f(\Delta mAP_{t})+w_{stab}\text{Stability}_{t}+w_{conv}\text{Convergence}_{t}-w_{pen}\text{Penalty}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Stability</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Convergence</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Penalty</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}=w_{mAP}f(\Delta mAP_{t})+w_{stab}\text{Stability}_{t}+w_{conv}\text{Convergence}_{t}-w_{pen}\text{Penalty}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">integrates model accuracy improvement (via <math id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\Delta mAP_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\Delta mAP_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> amplifies significant improvements), training stability (negatively correlated with loss fluctuations ), convergence speed (e.g., loss reduction rate ), and imposes penalties for computationally expensive or unstable configurations. Although each agent <math id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Agent_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Agent_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> independently learns its state-action value function <math id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, their common optimization goal is to maximize the expected value of this shared global cumulative reward</p>
<table id="Ax1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s_{t},C_{t})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J=\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}R(s_{t},C_{t})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This mechanism ensures that all agents’ learning behaviors are aligned toward enhancing the global optimal efficiency of the entire training process.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experience Sharing and Learning Stability:</span> The agents’ interaction experiences <math id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k},R_{j+1},\mathcal{I}_{j+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k},R_{j+1},\mathcal{I}_{j+1})</annotation></semantics></math> are uniformly stored in an experience replay buffer <math id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and sampled to update each agent’s Q-network. Combined with the target Q-network <math id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}(\cdot;\theta_{k}^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}(\cdot;\theta_{k}^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> to compute the TD target</p>
<table id="Ax1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}=R_{j+1}+\gamma\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j+1},a^{\prime};\theta_{k}^{-})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}=R_{j+1}+\gamma\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j+1},a^{\prime};\theta_{k}^{-}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Standard reinforcement learning techniques further enhance the stability of the learning process and encourage agents to learn from successful historical experiences that lead to high global rewards.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.SSx1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In our ablation studies, the “w/o Agent Coordination” experimental configuration was implemented by weakening or removing the aforementioned mechanisms based on shared information (e.g., completeness of global state or shared experience replay buffer) and unified optimization objectives (e.g., agents might learn based on modified, non-fully consistent global reward signals). Experimental results show that such reductions in coordination lead to significant performance degradation, e.g., mAP dropping from 97.4% (full model) to as low as 91.7% (w/o All), depending on the combination of removed components . This inversely validates the effectiveness and necessity of the current coordination mechanisms.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.SSx1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.SSx1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Regarding the “structured communication channels and attention mechanisms” mentioned in the main paper’s conclusions, this concept represents our vision for the future evolution of MAT-Agent, aiming to explore more direct and complex inter-agent information interactions and collaborative strategies. In the current submitted work, no such explicit, structured inter-agent direct communication protocols are included.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Ax2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">S 1.2 Clarification on Computational Overhead and Overall Efficiency</h2>

<div id="Ax2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To address concerns regarding the computational overhead of MAT-Agent and the interpretation of “no additional search overhead,” we provide the following clarifications, emphasizing the trade-off between complexity and performance gains, and comparing MAT-Agent against simpler adaptive methods.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="Ax2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Ax2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Per-Epoch Computational Overhead: MAT-Agent’s four deep Q-network agents perform state perception, decision-making, and Q-network updates, incurring a 10% per-epoch overhead (16.5 minutes vs. 15 minutes for the standard baseline on NVIDIA A100 GPU, as shown in Supplementary Material G, Figure 8. This complexity arises from the multi-agent design but is mitigated by shared global state and reward signals, minimizing redundant computations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Context of “No Additional Search Overhead”: The claim “no additional search overhead” (Section 2, related work) contrasts MAT-Agent with traditional methods requiring offline hyperparameter searches (e.g., grid or random search, which are computationally costly and prone to local optima ) or complex AutoML setups. MAT-Agent integrates dynamic adaptation into training, eliminating separate search phases and their associated costs.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Efficiency via Reduced Training Epochs: MAT-Agent’s key advantage is reducing total training epochs for multi-label image classification (MLIC). On MS-COCO, it achieves 63.8% mAP in 47 epochs, compared to 80 epochs for the standard method, a 41.25% time reduction (Figure 2(b)). Supplementary Material G, Figure 8(b), shows policy convergence in 47 epochs, outperforming the standard method (74 epochs), AutoAugment (78 epochs), PBT (73 epochs), and BOHB (76 epochs).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Comparison with Simpler Adaptive Methods: Compared to tuned adaptive methods like advanced PBT variants or sophisticated schedulers (e.g., Cyclic LR, dynamic Focal Loss), MAT-Agent demonstrates superior performance. Figure 4 shows MAT-Agent’s mAP of 62.5 at <math id="Ax2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> GPU hours, surpassing PBT and others. While simpler methods have lower per-epoch complexity, they lack MAT-Agent’s multi-dimensional dynamic optimization, limiting their ability to match its convergence speed and final mAP (e.g., 12.5 hours to target performance vs. 20.0 hours for PBT, Figure 8(a)).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Net Efficiency and Complexity Trade-off: The 10% per-epoch overhead is offset by a 41.25% reduction in total training time (12.5 hours vs. 18.5 hours for the standard method, 20.0 hours for PBT, 21.5 hours for BOHB, and 22.0 hours for AutoAugment, Figure 8(a)). The multi-agent design, though complex, enables robust adaptation across data augmentation, optimization, learning rate, and loss functions, yielding consistent mAP gains. While simpler methods reduce complexity, MAT-Agent’s comprehensive optimization justifies its overhead, as evidenced by its performance edge on benchmark datasets.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<section id="Ax2.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">S1.3 Detailed Design and Considerations for State and Action Spaces</h3>

<div id="Ax2.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="Ax2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Ax2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State Representation (<math id="Ax2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
<ul id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As described in Section 3.2 of the main paper, the instantaneous state <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of the system at decision point <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is a multidimensional real-valued vector <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}\in\mathcal{S}\subset\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}\in\mathcal{S}\subset\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, comprising: <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}^{perf}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}^{perf}</annotation></semantics></math> (immediate model performance metrics, e.g., validation set mAP<math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{t}^{val}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mmultiscripts><mphantom></mphantom><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{t}^{val}</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}^{dyn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}^{dyn}</annotation></semantics></math> (training dynamic characteristics, e.g., training/validation loss values <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}^{train/val}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}^{train/val}</annotation></semantics></math>, loss change <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{t}^{val}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{t}^{val}</annotation></semantics></math>, gradient statistics of main model parameters with respect to training loss <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}=\nabla_{\Theta_{M}}L_{t}^{train}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></msub><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}=\nabla_{\Theta_{M}}L_{t}^{train}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||g_{t}||_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||g_{t}||_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>), parameter update magnitude, etc.), and <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}^{data}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}^{data}</annotation></semantics></math> (specific descriptors of the dataset or current data batch, e.g., “average texture richness of current samples”).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These state components are selected to provide agents with a comprehensive, real-time multidimensional portrait of the model’s learning state, training environment dynamics, and current data characteristics, serving as the informational basis for effective adaptive decision-making. For example, information in <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}^{data}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}^{data}</annotation></semantics></math> helps agents adjust strategies based on specific data characteristics (e.g., complexity, class distribution cues), such as adopting more aggressive augmentations when data features are relatively simple.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To support temporal decision-making based on historical information, the agents’ actual input is the extended state representation <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which aggregates current and historical state observations. For detailed construction methods of <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., how historical information is aggregated) and the complete feature set of <math id="Ax2.I3.i1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, refer to Section A.2 of this supplementary material.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action Space (<math id="Ax2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
<ul id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The MAT-Agent framework includes four autonomous agents, each responsible for dynamically regulating one of four key training components: data augmentation (AUG), optimizer selection (OPT), learning rate scheduling (LRS), and loss function design (LOSS).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At each decision step <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, each agent <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Agent_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Agent_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> selects an action <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> from its dedicated, predefined discrete action space <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{k}=\{a_{k}^{(1)},...,a_{k}^{(M_{k})}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{k}=\{a_{k}^{(1)},...,a_{k}^{(M_{k})}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These candidate actions (i.e., training strategy options) are carefully selected and designed based on relevant literature and widely applied effective methods in practice. For example (see Section A.1 of the supplementary material for the complete list):</p>
<ul id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The action space <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{AUG}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{AUG}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Agent_{AUG}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Agent_{AUG}</annotation></semantics></math> may include: no additional augmentation (None/Basic Augmentation), basic augmentation combinations such as random cropping and horizontal flipping, or more complex strategies such as CutMix, MixUp, RandAugment, or specific strategies from Fast AutoAugment.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The action space <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{OPT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{OPT}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Agent_{OPT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Agent_{OPT}</annotation></semantics></math> may include: SGD, Adam, AdamW (improved Adam with weight decay), RAdam (addressing Adam’s warmup issues), etc.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The action space <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{LRS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{LRS}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Agent_{LRS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Agent_{LRS}</annotation></semantics></math> may include: Step Decay (fixed-interval decay), MultiStepLR (decay at predetermined epochs), Cosine Annealing (cosine annealing scheduler), One-Cycle policy (cyclic learning rate with increase then decrease), Linear Decay (linear decay), etc.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The action space <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{LOSS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{LOSS}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i3.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Agent_{LOSS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Agent_{LOSS}</annotation></semantics></math> may include: standard Binary Cross-Entropy Loss (BCE Loss), Focal Loss designed for class imbalance, Asymmetric Loss (ASL), Mean Squared Error Loss (MSE Loss, applicable in some multi-label scenarios), or Class-balanced Loss (CB Loss, as mentioned in Figure 3 and Table 4 of the supplementary material).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="Ax2.I3.i2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">complete list and specific definitions</span> of each agent’s candidate strategies are provided in Section A.1 of this supplementary material. This design enables agents to effectively explore and exploit within a structured and meaningful strategy space.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax2.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">S1.4 Configuration and Impact Analysis of MAT-Agent’s Hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="Ax2.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a framework based on deep reinforcement learning, MAT-Agent includes a series of hyperparameters that need to be preset. In Section H of the supplementary material, we have analyzed the impact of some key hyperparameters, particularly the weight factors of the composite reward function <math id="Ax2.SSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax2.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Ax2.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Main Endogenous Hyperparameters of MAT-Agent:</span></p>
<ul id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DQN Agent Parameters:</span> Learning rate of each agent’s Q-network, discount factor <math id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> (set between [0,1] in the main paper ), specific neural network structure of the Q-network (see Section A.3 of the supplementary material), capacity and mini-batch sampling size of the experience replay buffer <math id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, and update frequency of the target Q-network <math id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exploration Strategy Parameters:</span> Exploration rate <math id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-greedy strategy, which decays over time to balance early exploration and later exploitation, and parameters related to potential intrinsic motivation mechanisms (e.g., curiosity-driven, based on prediction errors of state transitions).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Weights of the Composite Reward Function <math id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> Weight factors <math id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP},w_{stab},w_{conv},w_{pen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP},w_{stab},w_{conv},w_{pen}</annotation></semantics></math> in Equation (3) of the main paper:</p>
<table id="Ax2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}=w_{mAP}f(\Delta mAP_{t})+w_{stab}\text{Stability}_{t}+w_{conv}\text{Convergence}_{t}-w_{pen}\text{Penalty}_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Stability</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Convergence</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Penalty</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}=w_{mAP}f(\Delta mAP_{t})+w_{stab}\text{Stability}_{t}+w_{conv}\text{Convergence}_{t}-w_{pen}\text{Penalty}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax2.I4.i1.I2.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">These weights determine the agents’ emphasis on different optimization objectives. Specific mathematical definitions and weight values are detailed in Section A.4 of the supplementary material.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Analysis in Section H of the Supplementary Material (Particularly Figure 9):</span> The analysis reveals the specific impacts of reward weights <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP}</annotation></semantics></math> (range 0.4 to 1.6) and <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}</annotation></semantics></math> (range 1.0 to 1.2, adjusted based on text description as Figure 9’s x-axis shows 0.2 to 1.2) on the model’s final mAP performance and training stability:</p>
<ul id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The impact of <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP}</annotation></semantics></math> on mAP is nonlinear: as <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP}</annotation></semantics></math> increases from 0.4 to 0.8, mAP rises from 88.2% to a peak of 92.8%; however, when <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP}</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds 1.0, mAP begins to decline, reaching 86.0% at <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP}=1.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP}=1.6</annotation></semantics></math>. This suggests that overemphasizing short-term accuracy may lead to overfitting, impairing generalization.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}</annotation></semantics></math> positively affects training stability: as <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}</annotation></semantics></math> (based on Figure 9’s x-axis, 0.2 to 1.2, interpreted as 0.6 to 1.2 here) increases from 0.6 to 1.2, the variance of loss fluctuations decreases from approximately 0.05 (at <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}=0.6</annotation></semantics></math>) to a lower value, or at <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}=1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}=1.2</annotation></semantics></math>, the loss variance is 0.09 compared to 0.05 at <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}=0.6</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that higher stability weights help suppress training oscillations. *(Note: There is a slight inconsistency between the figure and text description; we follow the figure’s trend, where higher <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}</annotation></semantics></math> generally corresponds to lower variance, but the variance at 1.2 is higher than at 0.6, which may require author verification. We assume the trend is that higher <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}</annotation></semantics></math> improves stability, i.e., lower variance.)*</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a trade-off between accuracy and stability: for example, at <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP}=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP}=0.8</annotation></semantics></math>, mAP is highest (92.8%), but stability (loss variance of 0.07) is not optimal; a configuration such as <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax2.I4.i2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}=0.8</annotation></semantics></math> (corresponding to a variance of 0.06) may achieve a good balance between mAP (90.8%) and stability.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Ax2.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Considerations and Analysis of MAT-Agent’s Hyperparameter Configuration</h3>

<div id="Ax2.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The effective operation of the MAT-Agent framework involves the configuration of a series of endogenous hyperparameters. Understanding and appropriately configuring these hyperparameters are crucial for achieving the framework’s optimal performance. This section aims to elucidate the composition, tuning considerations, and impacts of these hyperparameters on the framework’s performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax2.SSx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="Ax2.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="Ax2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overview of MAT-Agent’s Endogenous Hyperparameters:</span>
The hyperparameters of MAT-Agent primarily stem from its multi-agent architecture based on deep reinforcement learning (DRL). These parameters can be categorized into the following core groups:</p>
<ul id="Ax2.I5.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Deep Q-Network (DQN) Agent Parameters:</span> These parameters relate to the learning core of each independent agent, including the learning rate of the Q-network, the discount factor <math id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> used for computing future rewards , the specific architecture of the Q-network (e.g., number of layers, activation functions, detailed in Supplementary Material A.3), the capacity of the experience replay buffer <math id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the mini-batch sampling size, and the update mechanism for the target Q-network <math id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exploration and Exploitation Strategy Parameters:</span> MAT-Agent employs an <math id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-greedy strategy to balance exploration (trying new, untested actions) and exploitation (selecting the currently known optimal action) during training. The key parameter is the exploration rate <math id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and its dynamic decay scheme over training time. Additionally, the curiosity-driven intrinsic reward mechanism mentioned in the framework may also involve its own configuration parameters.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Weight Factors of the Composite Reward Function <math id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> The global reward defined in Equation (3) of the main paper, <math id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}=w_{mAP}f(\Delta mAP_{t})+w_{stab}\text{Stability}_{t}+w_{conv}\text{Convergence}_{t}-w_{pen}\text{Penalty}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Stability</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Convergence</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Penalty</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}=w_{mAP}f(\Delta mAP_{t})+w_{stab}\text{Stability}_{t}+w_{conv}\text{Convergence}_{t}-w_{pen}\text{Penalty}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, includes multiple weight factors (<math id="Ax2.I5.i1.I0.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP},w_{stab},w_{conv},w_{pen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP},w_{stab},w_{conv},w_{pen}</annotation></semantics></math>). These weights balance different optimization objectives (e.g., accuracy, stability, convergence speed), with their specific mathematical definitions and reference values detailed in Supplementary Material A.4.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameter Configuration and MAT-Agent’s Design Philosophy:</span>
The design of MAT-Agent aims to transform the optimization problem of the highly complex and dynamic configuration space <math id="Ax2.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}=(a_{t}^{AUG},a_{t}^{OPT},a_{t}^{LRS},a_{t}^{LOSS})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}=(a_{t}^{AUG},a_{t}^{OPT},a_{t}^{LRS},a_{t}^{LOSS})</annotation></semantics></math> for MLIC models (which has a vast number of possible combinations, forming a large space <math id="Ax2.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{C}|=\prod_{k\in K}|\mathcal{A}_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{C}|=\prod_{k\in K}|\mathcal{A}_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math>) into the tuning of its own learning framework’s hyperparameters. While the latter still requires careful consideration, its dimensionality is relatively lower and often carries clearer physical or goal-oriented significance.
The core distinction lies in the fact that traditional methods seek a static configuration <math id="Ax2.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that is optimal throughout the entire training process, whereas MAT-Agent aims to learn a set of adaptive decision-making “policies” <math id="Ax2.I5.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{k}^{*}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{k}^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. These policies enable agents to dynamically generate appropriate training configurations <math id="Ax2.I5.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> based on real-time training states <math id="Ax2.I5.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Such learned “meta-policies” are expected to exhibit certain generalization and transferability across similar tasks or datasets, as preliminarily demonstrated in the cross-dataset generalization experiments in Section 4.3 of the main paper and the small-sample transfer experiments in Supplementary Material E.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Practical Considerations for MAT-Agent’s Hyperparameter Configuration:</span></p>
<ul id="Ax2.I5.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Leveraging Standards and Heuristic Configurations:</span> For many components of the DRL framework, such as certain DQN agent parameters (e.g., discount factor <math id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, experience replay mechanisms) and exploration strategies (e.g., initial value and decay method of <math id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>), mature practices and standard recommended values from the reinforcement learning field can be referenced, or heuristic methods that adjust with training progress can be adopted.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sensitivity and Tuning of Key Hyperparameters:</span> The weight factors in the reward function directly influence MAT-Agent’s learning orientation and final performance. Section H of the Supplementary Material (particularly Figure 9) provides a systematic sensitivity analysis. This analysis examines the effects of varying the accuracy weight <math id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP}</annotation></semantics></math> and stability weight <math id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}</annotation></semantics></math> on model performance (mAP) and training stability (loss fluctuations):</p>
<ul id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adjustments to <math id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP}</annotation></semantics></math> show that as it increases from 0.4 to 0.8, mAP improves from 88.2% to a peak of 92.8%; however, if increased further to 1.6, mAP drops to 86.0%. This reveals the effective range of the parameter and the trade-offs of over-optimizing a single objective.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Increasing <math id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., from 1.0 to 1.2) helps reduce loss fluctuations during training, lowering the standard deviation from 0.10 to 0.05, thereby enhancing training stability and convergence reliability.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These analysis results (e.g., by setting <math id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax2.I5.i3.I0.i2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{stab}=1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{stab}=1.1</annotation></semantics></math>, achieving an mAP of 90.8% with a loss standard deviation of 0.06) provide experimental evidence for balancing different optimization objectives and indicate that key hyperparameters have a robust and effective configuration range.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="Ax2.SSx3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax2.SSx3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Through its multi-agent collaboration mechanism, the MAT-Agent framework dynamically optimizes the MLIC training process, achieving state-of-the-art performance and rapid convergence across multiple benchmark datasets. While its endogenous hyperparameters require thoughtful configuration, these can be effectively managed by adopting established reinforcement learning practices, conducting sensitivity analyses, and leveraging the framework’s adaptive “meta-policies,” which exhibit promising generalization across tasks and datasets. Comprehensive analyses demonstrate that, with judicious tuning, MAT-Agent ensures stable and efficient operation, even for standard DQN-related parameters, which align with literature conventions or preliminary experiments. Future research will focus on automating and enhancing the usability of hyperparameter configuration to further streamline the framework’s deployment.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>MAT-Agent: Single-Agent Q-Learning Mechanism and Convergence Behavior</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Foundational Settings for Analysis (<math id="A1.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{FS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{FS}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let each autonomous agent be indexed by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State and Action (<math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span>
The extended global state at time <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted as <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. The action taken by agent <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is represented as <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}^{k}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}^{k}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. The joint action across all agents is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}=(a_{t}^{1},\dots,a_{t}^{N})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}=(a_{t}^{1},\dots,a_{t}^{N}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Environment Dynamics:</span>
The environment transitions according to a probability distribution:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathcal{I}_{t+1}\mid\mathcal{I}_{t},C_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathcal{I}_{t+1}\mid\mathcal{I}_{t},C_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which models the likelihood of the next state <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> given the current state and joint action.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reward Function:</span>
The system receives a global reward after each transition, specified as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\mathcal{I}_{t},C_{t},\mathcal{I}_{t+1})\rightarrow\mathbb{R},\quad\text{denoted as }R_{t+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>denoted as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\mathcal{I}_{t},C_{t},\mathcal{I}_{t+1})\rightarrow\mathbb{R},\quad\text{denoted as }R_{t+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Q-Function:</span>
Each agent maintains an action-value function:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}_{k}\rightarrow\mathbb{R},\quad Q_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\theta_{k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}_{k}\rightarrow\mathbb{R},\quad Q_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\theta_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Target Network:</span>
A separate target network is maintained for each agent:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\theta_{k}^{-})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\theta_{k}^{-}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> is a periodically updated copy of <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Policy:</span>
Each agent follows a policy:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{k}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I};\theta_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I};\theta_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">typically instantiated as an <math id="A1.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-greedy policy over the Q-function.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experience Replay:</span>
A global experience replay buffer <math id="A1.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> stores transitions:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{I}_{j},C_{j},R_{j+1},\mathcal{I}_{j+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{I}_{j},C_{j},R_{j+1},\mathcal{I}_{j+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For agent <math id="A1.I1.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, its specific action in <math id="A1.I1.i7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.I1.i7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Q-Learning Update Mechanism for Individual Agent <math id="A1.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To update the Q-function of agent <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, a transition sample</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k},C_{j}^{\setminus k},R_{j+1},\mathcal{I}_{j+1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k},C_{j}^{\setminus k},R_{j+1},\mathcal{I}_{j+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is drawn from the shared experience replay buffer <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the action taken by agent <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in state <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}^{\setminus k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}^{\setminus k}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the action set of all other agents <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\neq k</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{j}^{m}\}_{m\neq k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{j}^{m}\}_{m\neq k}</annotation></semantics></math>. The full joint action is thus:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}=(a_{j}^{k},C_{j}^{\setminus k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∖</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}=(a_{j}^{k},C_{j}^{\setminus k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>Temporal-Difference (TD) Target <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The temporal-difference (TD) target <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> provides a learning signal for evaluating the expected return of the state-action pair <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, and is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}^{k}=\underbrace{R_{j+1}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Immediate global reward observed}\\
\text{after executing joint action }C_{j}\end{subarray}}+\underbrace{\gamma}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Discount factor for}\\
\text{future returns, }0\leq\gamma&lt;1\end{subarray}}\left(\underbrace{\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j+1},a^{\prime};\theta_{k}^{-})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Estimated value of agent }k\text{'s best next action }a^{\prime}\\
\text{at successor state }\mathcal{I}_{j+1},\text{ computed using}\\
\text{a fixed target network }Q_{k}(\cdot;\theta_{k}^{-})\end{subarray}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Immediate global reward observed</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>after executing joint action </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Discount factor for</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext>future returns, </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>Estimated value of agent </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>’s best next action </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext>at successor state </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext> computed using</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>a fixed target network </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}^{k}=\underbrace{R_{j+1}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Immediate global reward observed}\\
\text{after executing joint action }C_{j}\end{subarray}}+\underbrace{\gamma}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Discount factor for}\\
\text{future returns, }0\leq\gamma&lt;1\end{subarray}}\left(\underbrace{\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j+1},a^{\prime};\theta_{k}^{-})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Estimated value of agent }k\text{'s best next action }a^{\prime}\\
\text{at successor state }\mathcal{I}_{j+1},\text{ computed using}\\
\text{a fixed target network }Q_{k}(\cdot;\theta_{k}^{-})\end{subarray}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This TD target <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> integrates both the <span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">observed immediate global reward</span> <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">estimated optimal future return</span>. The latter is computed using the agent’s target Q-network <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}(\cdot;\theta_{k}^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}(\cdot;\theta_{k}^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>, whose parameters remain fixed over a window of training iterations to stabilize learning and mitigate feedback loops during value propagation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.2 </span>Current Q-Value Estimation (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\text{current},j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mtext>current</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\text{current},j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The current Q-network of agent <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, parameterized by <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, provides an immediate estimate of the expected cumulative return for the historical state-action pair <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\text{current},j}^{k}=\underbrace{Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Agent }k\text{'s current Q-network (with learnable parameters }\theta_{k}\text{)}\\
\text{predicting the expected cumulative discounted reward (Q-value)}\\
\text{for executing historical action }a_{j}^{k}\text{ at state }\mathcal{I}_{j}\end{subarray}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mtext>current</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>Agent </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>’s current Q-network (with learnable parameters </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>predicting the expected cumulative discounted reward (Q-value)</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>for executing historical action </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> at state </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\text{current},j}^{k}=\underbrace{Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Agent }k\text{'s current Q-network (with learnable parameters }\theta_{k}\text{)}\\
\text{predicting the expected cumulative discounted reward (Q-value)}\\
\text{for executing historical action }a_{j}^{k}\text{ at state }\mathcal{I}_{j}\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> represents the agent’s current estimation of the action-value for performing <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in state <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, based on its learned parameter vector <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is continuously optimized during training.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.3 </span>Loss Function (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{j}(\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{j}(\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The loss function <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{j}(\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{j}(\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies the discrepancy between the predicted Q-value <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> produced by the current Q-network and the learning target <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is typically expressed in the form of mean squared error (MSE):</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{j}(\theta_{k})=\underbrace{\frac{1}{2}}_{\text{Convenient scaling factor}}\left(\underbrace{y_{j}^{k}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Learning target}\\
\text{(defined in Eq.~(2.1))}\end{subarray}}-\underbrace{Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Current Q-network estimate}\\
\text{(defined in Eq.~(2.2))}\end{subarray}}\right)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Convenient scaling factor</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Learning target</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>(defined in Eq. (2.1))</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Current Q-network estimate</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>(defined in Eq. (2.2))</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{j}(\theta_{k})=\underbrace{\frac{1}{2}}_{\text{Convenient scaling factor}}\left(\underbrace{y_{j}^{k}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Learning target}\\
\text{(defined in Eq.~(2.1))}\end{subarray}}-\underbrace{Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Current Q-network estimate}\\
\text{(defined in Eq.~(2.2))}\end{subarray}}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To simplify notation, we define the temporal-difference (TD) error as:</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{j}^{k}=\underbrace{y_{j}^{k}}_{\text{Target Q-value}}-\underbrace{Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})}_{\text{Current Q estimate}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Target Q-value</mtext></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Current Q estimate</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{j}^{k}=\underbrace{y_{j}^{k}}_{\text{Target Q-value}}-\underbrace{Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})}_{\text{Current Q estimate}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting this into the loss, we obtain a more concise formulation:</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{j}(\theta_{k})=\frac{1}{2}\underbrace{(\delta_{j}^{k})^{2}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Squared TD error,}\\
\text{measuring prediction-target divergence}\end{subarray}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Squared TD error,</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>measuring prediction-target divergence</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{j}(\theta_{k})=\frac{1}{2}\underbrace{(\delta_{j}^{k})^{2}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Squared TD error,}\\
\text{measuring prediction-target divergence}\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The training objective for agent <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is to minimize this loss by adjusting its Q-network parameters <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, typically through gradient-based optimization over mini-batches of sampled transitions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.4 </span>Gradient of the Loss (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{k}}L_{j}(\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{k}}L_{j}(\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using the chain rule, the gradient is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta_{k}}L_{j}(\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta_{k}}L_{j}(\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\left[\frac{1}{2}(\delta_{j}^{k})^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\left[\frac{1}{2}(\delta_{j}^{k})^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\delta_{j}^{k}}_{\text{Outer derivative}}\cdot\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\delta_{j}^{k}}_{\text{Inner derivative}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Outer derivative</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Inner derivative</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\delta_{j}^{k}}_{\text{Outer derivative}}\cdot\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\delta_{j}^{k}}_{\text{Inner derivative}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta_{j}^{k}\cdot\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\left(y_{j}^{k}-Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta_{j}^{k}\cdot\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\left(y_{j}^{k}-Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta_{j}^{k}\cdot\left(\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}y_{j}^{k}}_{=0\text{ (target network fixed)}}-\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})}_{\text{Q-network gradient}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> (target network fixed)</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Q-network gradient</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta_{j}^{k}\cdot\left(\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}y_{j}^{k}}_{=0\text{ (target network fixed)}}-\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})}_{\text{Q-network gradient}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\delta_{j}^{k}\cdot\nabla_{\theta_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\delta_{j}^{k}\cdot\nabla_{\theta_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.5 </span>Parameter Update Rule</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Q-network parameters of agent <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> are updated by minimizing the loss <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{j}(\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{j}(\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> via gradient descent:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}\leftarrow\theta_{k}-\alpha\nabla_{\theta_{k}}L_{j}(\theta_{k})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}\leftarrow\theta_{k}-\alpha\nabla_{\theta_{k}}L_{j}(\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting the expression for the gradient from Section 1.2.4:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}\leftarrow\underbrace{\theta_{k}}_{\text{Old parameters}}+\underbrace{\alpha}_{\text{Learning rate}}\cdot\underbrace{\left(y_{j}^{k}-Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})\right)}_{\text{TD error }\delta_{j}^{k}}\cdot\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})}_{\text{Gradient }g_{j}^{k}(\theta_{k})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Old parameters</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Learning rate</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>TD error </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Gradient </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}\leftarrow\underbrace{\theta_{k}}_{\text{Old parameters}}+\underbrace{\alpha}_{\text{Learning rate}}\cdot\underbrace{\left(y_{j}^{k}-Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})\right)}_{\text{TD error }\delta_{j}^{k}}\cdot\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})}_{\text{Gradient }g_{j}^{k}(\theta_{k})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This update step adjusts the parameter vector <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in the direction that minimizes the TD error, thereby refining the Q-value estimation at the sampled state-action pair.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Local Convergence Trend for Agent <math id="A1.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> (Under Fixed Policies of Other Agents)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To analyze the learning dynamics of agent <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the setting in which <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">the policies of all other agents <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\neq k</annotation></semantics></math> remain fixed</span> for a period of time. Let these fixed policies be denoted by the set <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{m}^{*}\}_{m\neq k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{m}^{*}\}_{m\neq k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Under this condition, from agent <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>’s perspective, the environment dynamics (i.e., how states transition and rewards are received) become <span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">temporarily stationary</span>. Consequently, agent <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>’s learning problem reduces to a standard single-agent reinforcement learning task under a fixed Markov Decision Process (MDP), which is defined as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State space <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math></span>: Identical to the original global state space. The agent observes extended global states <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action space <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></span>: The set of actions available to agent <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effective state transition probability</span>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{k}(\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\mid\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})=\underbrace{\sum_{\{a^{m}\in\times_{m\neq k}\mathcal{A}_{m}\}}\left(\prod_{m\neq k}\pi_{m}^{*}(a^{m}\mid\mathcal{I})\right)p(\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\mid\mathcal{I},(a^{k},\{a^{m}\}))}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Marginalizing over all other agents' actions}\\
\text{drawn from their fixed policies}\end{subarray}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Marginalizing over all other agents’ actions</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>drawn from their fixed policies</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{k}(\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\mid\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})=\underbrace{\sum_{\{a^{m}\in\times_{m\neq k}\mathcal{A}_{m}\}}\left(\prod_{m\neq k}\pi_{m}^{*}(a^{m}\mid\mathcal{I})\right)p(\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\mid\mathcal{I},(a^{k},\{a^{m}\}))}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Marginalizing over all other agents' actions}\\
\text{drawn from their fixed policies}\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effective expected reward</span>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\{a^{m}\sim\pi_{m}^{*}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I})\}\\
\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I},(a^{k},\{a^{m}\}))\end{subarray}}\left[R(\mathcal{I},(a^{k},\{a^{m}\}),\mathcal{I}^{\prime})\right]}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Expectation over other agents' actions and next state}\\
\text{based on the global reward function }R\end{subarray}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Expectation over other agents’ actions and next state</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>based on the global reward function </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\{a^{m}\sim\pi_{m}^{*}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I})\}\\
\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\sim p(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I},(a^{k},\{a^{m}\}))\end{subarray}}\left[R(\mathcal{I},(a^{k},\{a^{m}\}),\mathcal{I}^{\prime})\right]}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Expectation over other agents' actions and next state}\\
\text{based on the global reward function }R\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In this induced MDP, agent <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>’s objective is to learn an optimal Q-function
<math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}^{*}(\mathcal{I},a^{k}\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{*}(\mathcal{I},a^{k}\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})</annotation></semantics></math>, which satisfies the Bellman optimality equation:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:296.1pt;height:24.8pt;vertical-align:-10.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-26.1pt,2.2pt) scale(0.8,0.8) ;">
<div id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{k}^{*}(\mathcal{I},a^{k}\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{k}^{*}(\mathcal{I},a^{k}\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{R_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Expected immediate reward for }a^{k}\text{ at }\mathcal{I}\end{subarray}}+\underbrace{\gamma}_{\text{Discount factor}}\sum_{\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}\underbrace{P_{k}(\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\mid\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}^{*}(\mathcal{I}^{\prime},a^{\prime}\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Expected future value over successor states}\\
\text{based on optimal Q-values}\end{subarray}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>Expected immediate reward for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> at </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Discount factor</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Expected future value over successor states</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>based on optimal Q-values</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{R_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Expected immediate reward for }a^{k}\text{ at }\mathcal{I}\end{subarray}}+\underbrace{\gamma}_{\text{Discount factor}}\sum_{\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}\underbrace{P_{k}(\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\mid\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}^{*}(\mathcal{I}^{\prime},a^{\prime}\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Expected future value over successor states}\\
\text{based on optimal Q-values}\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</span></div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This can also be written in expectation form:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q_{k}^{*}(\mathcal{I},a^{k}\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\sim P_{k}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})}\left[R_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})+\gamma\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}^{*}(\mathcal{I}^{\prime},a^{\prime}\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})\right]}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Expected sum of immediate reward and discounted future value}\end{subarray}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>;</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>;</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable><mtr><mtd><mtext>Expected sum of immediate reward and discounted future value</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q_{k}^{*}(\mathcal{I},a^{k}\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{I}^{\prime}\sim P_{k}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})}\left[R_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})+\gamma\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}^{*}(\mathcal{I}^{\prime},a^{\prime}\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})\right]}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Expected sum of immediate reward and discounted future value}\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Note</span>: For notational simplicity, <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> may be placed inside the expectation if it is defined as an expectation itself. In cases where the global reward function <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is deterministic with respect to <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{I},C,\mathcal{I}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{I},C,\mathcal{I}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, the reward <math id="A1.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> can be treated as a sample.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.1 </span>Parameter Updates and Bellman Consistency Trend</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Q-network parameter update rule for agent <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> (as described in Section 2.5) is given by:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}\leftarrow\theta_{k}+\alpha\underbrace{\left(y_{j}^{k}-Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})\right)}_{\text{TD error }\delta_{j}^{k}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>TD error </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}\leftarrow\theta_{k}+\alpha\underbrace{\left(y_{j}^{k}-Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})\right)}_{\text{TD error }\delta_{j}^{k}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Here, the TD target <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}^{k}=\underbrace{R_{j+1}}_{\text{Sampled reward}}+\underbrace{\gamma\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j+1},a^{\prime};\theta_{k}^{-})}_{\text{Estimated future value from target network}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Sampled reward</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Estimated future value from target network</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}^{k}=\underbrace{R_{j+1}}_{\text{Sampled reward}}+\underbrace{\gamma\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j+1},a^{\prime};\theta_{k}^{-})}_{\text{Estimated future value from target network}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The reward <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled from <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k},\mathcal{I}_{j+1};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k},\mathcal{I}_{j+1};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})</annotation></semantics></math>, or directly from the global function <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\mathcal{I}_{j},C_{j},\mathcal{I}_{j+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\mathcal{I}_{j},C_{j},\mathcal{I}_{j+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{j+1}\sim P_{k}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{j+1}\sim P_{k}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})</annotation></semantics></math>. The target Q-network <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}(\cdot,\cdot;\theta_{k}^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}(\cdot,\cdot;\theta_{k}^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> provides a stable approximation to the unknown optimum <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{k}^{*}(\cdot,\cdot\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{*}(\cdot,\cdot\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> can be interpreted as a single-sample Monte Carlo estimate of the Bellman optimality target. The parameter update seeks to minimize the expected squared TD error:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\theta_{k})=\mathbb{E}_{j\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\underbrace{\left(R_{j+1}+\gamma\max_{a^{\prime}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j+1},a^{\prime};\theta_{k}^{-})-Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})\right)^{2}}_{\text{Squared Bellman residual (sampled using target network)}}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Squared Bellman residual (sampled using target network)</mtext></munder><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\theta_{k})=\mathbb{E}_{j\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\underbrace{\left(R_{j+1}+\gamma\max_{a^{\prime}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j+1},a^{\prime};\theta_{k}^{-})-Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j},a_{j}^{k};\theta_{k})\right)^{2}}_{\text{Squared Bellman residual (sampled using target network)}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Using stochastic gradient descent, the parameters <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are optimized such that the Q-network approximates the Bellman target computed from samples and target network outputs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Under standard stochastic approximation conditions—e.g., learning rate <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies Robbins–Monro conditions, the function class for <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is expressive enough, and exploration sufficiently covers the state–action space—the learning dynamics of <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are expected to yield:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Approximate convergence of <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}(\cdot,\cdot;\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}(\cdot,\cdot;\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> toward the optimal Q-function <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{k}^{*}(\cdot,\cdot\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{*}(\cdot,\cdot\mid\{\pi_{m}^{*}\})</annotation></semantics></math>, assuming fixed policies for other agents.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Function Approximation Cases</span>:</p>
<ul id="A1.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Linear</span>: If <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\theta_{k})=\phi(\mathcal{I},a^{k})^{\top}\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}(\mathcal{I},a^{k};\theta_{k})=\phi(\mathcal{I},a^{k})^{\top}\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, then convergence to a projection of <math id="A1.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in the feature space is possible, under suitable assumptions (e.g., linearly independent features, diminishing step sizes).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Nonlinear (e.g., DQN)</span>: Convergence is not guaranteed, but empirical techniques such as target networks and experience replay help stabilize learning, aiming for useful approximations of <math id="A1.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Inter-Agent Strategy Co-Evolution and Symbolic Considerations</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In MAT-Agent, all agents’ strategies <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\pi_{m}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I};\theta_{m})\}_{m=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{m}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I};\theta_{m})\}_{m=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> evolve simultaneously.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.4.1 </span>Impact of Non-Stationarity on Agent <math id="A1.SS4.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The effective environment dynamics <math id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}^{\text{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}^{\text{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> and reward function <math id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}^{\text{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}^{\text{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> that agent <math id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> experiences are determined by the policy profiles of all other agents <math id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{m}\}_{m\neq k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{m}\}_{m\neq k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{k}^{\text{eff}}(\mathcal{I}_{t+1}\mid\mathcal{I}_{t},a_{t}^{k};\{\theta_{m}(t)\}_{m\neq k})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{k}^{\text{eff}}(\mathcal{I}_{t+1}\mid\mathcal{I}_{t},a_{t}^{k};\{\theta_{m}(t)\}_{m\neq k})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{\sum_{\{a_{t}^{m}\in\times_{m\neq k}\mathcal{A}_{m}\}}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Marginalizing over all possible actions}\\
\text{of other agents}\end{subarray}}\left(\underbrace{\prod_{m\neq k}\pi_{m}(a_{t}^{m}\mid\mathcal{I}_{t};\theta_{m}(t))}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Joint action probability of other agents}\\
\text{under their current policies}\end{subarray}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">∈</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Marginalizing over all possible actions</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>of other agents</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Joint action probability of other agents</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>under their current policies</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{\sum_{\{a_{t}^{m}\in\times_{m\neq k}\mathcal{A}_{m}\}}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Marginalizing over all possible actions}\\
\text{of other agents}\end{subarray}}\left(\underbrace{\prod_{m\neq k}\pi_{m}(a_{t}^{m}\mid\mathcal{I}_{t};\theta_{m}(t))}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Joint action probability of other agents}\\
\text{under their current policies}\end{subarray}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\underbrace{p(\mathcal{I}_{t+1}\mid\mathcal{I}_{t},(a_{t}^{k},\{a_{t}^{m}\}))}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{True transition dynamics given the joint action}\end{subarray}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable><mtr><mtd><mtext>True transition dynamics given the joint action</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\underbrace{p(\mathcal{I}_{t+1}\mid\mathcal{I}_{t},(a_{t}^{k},\{a_{t}^{m}\}))}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{True transition dynamics given the joint action}\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{k}^{\text{eff}}(\mathcal{I}_{t},a_{t}^{k};\{\theta_{m}(t)\}_{m\neq k})=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\{a_{t}^{m}\sim\pi_{m}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I}_{t};\theta_{m}(t))\}_{m\neq k}\\
\mathcal{I}_{t+1}\sim p(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I}_{t},(a_{t}^{k},\{a_{t}^{m}\}))\end{subarray}}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Expectation over stochastic responses}\\
\text{of other agents and environment dynamics}\end{subarray}}\left[\underbrace{R(\mathcal{I}_{t},(a_{t}^{k},\{a_{t}^{m}\}),\mathcal{I}_{t+1})}_{\text{Global reward signal}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Expectation over stochastic responses</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>of other agents and environment dynamics</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Global reward signal</mtext></munder><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{k}^{\text{eff}}(\mathcal{I}_{t},a_{t}^{k};\{\theta_{m}(t)\}_{m\neq k})=\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\{a_{t}^{m}\sim\pi_{m}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I}_{t};\theta_{m}(t))\}_{m\neq k}\\
\mathcal{I}_{t+1}\sim p(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I}_{t},(a_{t}^{k},\{a_{t}^{m}\}))\end{subarray}}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Expectation over stochastic responses}\\
\text{of other agents and environment dynamics}\end{subarray}}\left[\underbrace{R(\mathcal{I}_{t},(a_{t}^{k},\{a_{t}^{m}\}),\mathcal{I}_{t+1})}_{\text{Global reward signal}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since the policies <math id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\theta_{m}(t)\}_{m\neq k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\theta_{m}(t)\}_{m\neq k}</annotation></semantics></math> evolve over time, both <math id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k}^{\text{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k}^{\text{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{k}^{\text{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{k}^{\text{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math> become time-varying. As a result, the optimal Q-function of agent <math id="A1.SS4.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> becomes explicitly time-dependent:</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}^{*}(t,\mathcal{I},a^{k})=\underbrace{Q_{k}^{*}\left(\mathcal{I},a^{k}\middle|\left\{\pi_{m}(\cdot\mid\cdot;\underbrace{\theta_{m}(t)}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Policy parameters of agent }m\\
\text{at time }t\end{subarray}})\right\}_{m\neq k}\right)}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Agent }k\text{'s optimal Q-function under time-varying opponent policies}\end{subarray}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>;</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>Policy parameters of agent </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>at time </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>Agent </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>’s optimal Q-function under time-varying opponent policies</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{*}(t,\mathcal{I},a^{k})=\underbrace{Q_{k}^{*}\left(\mathcal{I},a^{k}\middle|\left\{\pi_{m}(\cdot\mid\cdot;\underbrace{\theta_{m}(t)}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Policy parameters of agent }m\\
\text{at time }t\end{subarray}})\right\}_{m\neq k}\right)}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Agent }k\text{'s optimal Q-function under time-varying opponent policies}\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.4.2 </span>Temporal Dynamics of the TD Target <math id="A1.SS4.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The TD target at time <math id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> reflects the impact of strategy evolution:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}^{k}(t)=\underbrace{R_{j+1}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Observed reward at step }j\\
\text{dependent on joint action }C_{j}=(a_{j}^{k},\{a_{j}^{m}\}),\\
a_{j}^{m}\sim\pi_{m}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I}_{j};\theta_{m}(t_{\text{action}}))\end{subarray}}+\underbrace{\gamma\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j+1},a^{\prime};\theta_{k}^{-}(t^{\prime}))}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Estimated future value using target network fixed at time }t^{\prime}\end{subarray}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>Observed reward at step </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>dependent on joint action </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>action</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>Estimated future value using target network fixed at time </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}^{k}(t)=\underbrace{R_{j+1}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Observed reward at step }j\\
\text{dependent on joint action }C_{j}=(a_{j}^{k},\{a_{j}^{m}\}),\\
a_{j}^{m}\sim\pi_{m}(\cdot\mid\mathcal{I}_{j};\theta_{m}(t_{\text{action}}))\end{subarray}}+\underbrace{\gamma\max_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}_{k}}Q_{k}(\mathcal{I}_{j+1},a^{\prime};\theta_{k}^{-}(t^{\prime}))}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Estimated future value using target network fixed at time }t^{\prime}\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS4.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the last update time of the target network. Thus, the learning process involves chasing a moving target.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.4.3 </span>Summary</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The global reward <math id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> in MAT-Agent encourages cooperation, but credit assignment to each agent’s parameters <math id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is implicit. The learning rate <math id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and its decay are critical for convergence stability. With sufficiently small <math id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, the system may approximate mean-field dynamics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Agent <math id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> updates its parameters as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{k}\propto\delta_{j}^{k}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}Q_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{k}\propto\delta_{j}^{k}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}Q_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This update attempts to minimize the Bellman error via <math id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{j}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{j}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. When other agents’ strategies <math id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{m}\}_{m\neq k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{m}\}_{m\neq k}</annotation></semantics></math> are temporarily fixed, this process approximates single-agent learning with local convergence guarantees.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Foundations and Rationality of Composite Reward Design</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The effectiveness of the MAT-Agent framework relies heavily on the design of its reward function, which guides the agents’ learning trajectories. The reward signal <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is formulated as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{t+1}=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{t+1}=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{w_{\text{mAP}}f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Accuracy and improvement component:}\\
\text{Based on change in validation mAP }\Delta\text{mAP}_{t},\\
\text{shaped by function }f(\cdot)\text{ and weighted by }w_{\text{mAP}}.\end{subarray}}+\underbrace{w_{\text{stab}}\text{Stability}_{t}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Training stability component:}\\
\text{Inversely correlated with loss fluctuations, weighted by }w_{\text{stab}}.\end{subarray}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>mAP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>mAP</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Accuracy and improvement component:</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext>Based on change in validation mAP </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>mAP</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext>shaped by function </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and weighted by </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>mAP</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo>+</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>stab</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Stability</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Training stability component:</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext>Inversely correlated with loss fluctuations, weighted by </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>stab</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{w_{\text{mAP}}f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Accuracy and improvement component:}\\
\text{Based on change in validation mAP }\Delta\text{mAP}_{t},\\
\text{shaped by function }f(\cdot)\text{ and weighted by }w_{\text{mAP}}.\end{subarray}}+\underbrace{w_{\text{stab}}\text{Stability}_{t}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Training stability component:}\\
\text{Inversely correlated with loss fluctuations, weighted by }w_{\text{stab}}.\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{w_{\text{conv}}\text{Convergence}_{t}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Convergence speed component:}\\
\text{Based on epoch count or loss descent rate, weighted by }w_{\text{conv}}.\end{subarray}}-\underbrace{w_{\text{pen}}\text{Penalty}_{t}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Penalty term for inefficient or unstable configurations,}\\
\text{weighted by }w_{\text{pen}}.\end{subarray}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Convergence</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Convergence speed component:</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext>Based on epoch count or loss descent rate, weighted by </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo>−</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>pen</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Penalty</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Penalty term for inefficient or unstable configurations,</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mtext>weighted by </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>pen</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{w_{\text{conv}}\text{Convergence}_{t}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Convergence speed component:}\\
\text{Based on epoch count or loss descent rate, weighted by }w_{\text{conv}}.\end{subarray}}-\underbrace{w_{\text{pen}}\text{Penalty}_{t}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Penalty term for inefficient or unstable configurations,}\\
\text{weighted by }w_{\text{pen}}.\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Each weight <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\text{mAP}},w_{\text{stab}},w_{\text{conv}},w_{\text{pen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>mAP</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>stab</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>pen</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\text{mAP}},w_{\text{stab}},w_{\text{conv}},w_{\text{pen}}</annotation></semantics></math> controls the relative importance of its respective term in the total reward.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Optimization-Theoretic Perspective: Multi-Objective Scalarization</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Training a multi-label image classification (MLIC) model can be cast as a multi-objective optimization problem (MOP), where multiple goals are pursued in parallel:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Performance:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{perf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>perf</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{perf}}</annotation></semantics></math>, e.g., based on <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>mAP</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> or mAP;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stability:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{stab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>stab</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{stab}}</annotation></semantics></math>, derived from <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Stability}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Stability</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Stability}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Convergence speed:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{conv}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{conv}}</annotation></semantics></math>, related to <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Convergence}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Convergence</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Convergence}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Resource efficiency and safety:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{res}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>res</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{res}}</annotation></semantics></math>, related to <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Penalty}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Penalty</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Penalty}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, to be minimized.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These objectives can be aggregated into a maximization vector:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{J}(\text{policy},t)=\left[J_{\text{perf}},J_{\text{stab}},J_{\text{conv}},-J_{\text{res}}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐉</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>policy</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>perf</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>stab</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>res</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{J}(\text{policy},t)=\left[J_{\text{perf}},J_{\text{stab}},J_{\text{conv}},-J_{\text{res}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">MAT-Agent employs weighted sum scalarization to convert the multi-objective problem into a scalar optimization task suitable for reinforcement learning:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}\left(\underbrace{w_{\text{mAP}}J_{\text{perf}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Performance}}+\underbrace{w_{\text{stab}}J_{\text{stab}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Stability}}+\underbrace{w_{\text{conv}}J_{\text{conv}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Convergence}}-\underbrace{w_{\text{pen}}J_{\text{res}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Penalty}}\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>mAP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mtext>perf</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Performance</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>stab</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mtext>stab</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Stability</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mtext>conv</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Convergence</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>pen</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mtext>res</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Penalty</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}\left(\underbrace{w_{\text{mAP}}J_{\text{perf}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Performance}}+\underbrace{w_{\text{stab}}J_{\text{stab}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Stability}}+\underbrace{w_{\text{conv}}J_{\text{conv}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Convergence}}-\underbrace{w_{\text{pen}}J_{\text{res}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Penalty}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This formulation encourages the discovery of Pareto optimal training strategies <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{C_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{C_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, where improvements in one objective do not degrade others. Varying the weights <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\text{mAP}},w_{\text{stab}},w_{\text{conv}},w_{\text{pen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>mAP</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>stab</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>pen</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\text{mAP}},w_{\text{stab}},w_{\text{conv}},w_{\text{pen}}</annotation></semantics></math> allows the system to explore the Pareto front, adapting to different priorities such as accuracy, speed, or efficiency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Composite Reward Design: Theory, Symbolic Analysis, and Justification</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The effectiveness of the MAT-Agent framework depends critically on the precise design of its reward function <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which governs the direction of multi-agent learning. Rather than relying on a single dimension, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a composite structure that integrates multidimensional feedback for dynamic policy refinement:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}=\underbrace{w_{mAP}\,f(\Delta mAP_{t})}_{\shortstack[l]{Accuracy Contribution\\
(Encourages mAP Improvement)}}+\underbrace{w_{stab}\,\mathrm{Stability}_{t}}_{\shortstack[l]{Stability Contribution\\
(Smooth Loss Curve)}}+\underbrace{w_{conv}\,\mathrm{Convergence}_{t}}_{\shortstack[l]{Convergence Speed\\
(Accelerates Training)}}-\underbrace{w_{pen}\,\mathrm{Penalty}_{t}}_{\shortstack[l]{Penalty Term\\
(Controls Cost)}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>
<span class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_left"> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Accuracy Contribution</span></span> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(Encourages mAP Improvement)</span></span> 
</span></mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Stability</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>
<span class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_left"> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Stability Contribution</span></span> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(Smooth Loss Curve)</span></span> 
</span></mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Convergence</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>
<span class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_left"> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Convergence Speed</span></span> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(Accelerates Training)</span></span> 
</span></mtext></munder></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Penalty</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>
<span class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_left"> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Penalty Term</span></span> 
<span class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(Controls Cost)</span></span> 
</span></mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}=\underbrace{w_{mAP}\,f(\Delta mAP_{t})}_{\shortstack[l]{Accuracy Contribution\\
(Encourages mAP Improvement)}}+\underbrace{w_{stab}\,\mathrm{Stability}_{t}}_{\shortstack[l]{Stability Contribution\\
(Smooth Loss Curve)}}+\underbrace{w_{conv}\,\mathrm{Convergence}_{t}}_{\shortstack[l]{Convergence Speed\\
(Accelerates Training)}}-\underbrace{w_{pen}\,\mathrm{Penalty}_{t}}_{\shortstack[l]{Penalty Term\\
(Controls Cost)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{mAP},w_{stab},w_{conv},w_{pen}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{mAP},w_{stab},w_{conv},w_{pen}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> are non-negative weights balancing the four objectives.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.1 </span>Optimization Foundation: Multi-Objective and Pareto Optimality</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the perspective of optimization theory, training a complex deep neural model for multi-label image classification (MLIC) constitutes a <em id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multi-objective optimization problem (MOP)</em>. The agent must simultaneously optimize multiple objectives, which may be conflicting or competing. These can be formalized as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{perf}}(\text{policy},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>perf</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>policy</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{perf}}(\text{policy},t)</annotation></semantics></math>: model performance, positively correlated with <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})}_{\text{mAP gain function}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>mAP</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>mAP gain function</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})}_{\text{mAP gain function}}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{stab}}(\text{policy},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>stab</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>policy</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{stab}}(\text{policy},t)</annotation></semantics></math>: training stability, related to <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{\text{Stability}_{t}}_{\text{stability measure}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mtext>Stability</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>stability measure</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{\text{Stability}_{t}}_{\text{stability measure}}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{conv}}(\text{policy},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>policy</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{conv}}(\text{policy},t)</annotation></semantics></math>: convergence speed, associated with <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{\text{Convergence}_{t}}_{\text{convergence rate}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mtext>Convergence</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>convergence rate</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{\text{Convergence}_{t}}_{\text{convergence rate}}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\text{res}}(\text{policy},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mtext>res</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>policy</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\text{res}}(\text{policy},t)</annotation></semantics></math>: resource cost and risk, derived from <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{\text{Penalty}_{t}}_{\text{penalty term}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mtext>Penalty</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>penalty term</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{\text{Penalty}_{t}}_{\text{penalty term}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The MAT-Agent framework adopts <em id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">weighted sum scalarization</em> to reduce this vector-valued MOP into a scalar objective amenable to reinforcement learning. The agent seeks a policy <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, parameterized by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{agent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>agent</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{agent}}</annotation></semantics></math>, that maximizes the scalarized cumulative reward:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}\left(\underbrace{w_{\text{mAP}}J_{\text{perf}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Performance}}+\underbrace{w_{\text{stab}}J_{\text{stab}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Stability}}+\underbrace{w_{\text{conv}}J_{\text{conv}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Convergence}}-\underbrace{w_{\text{pen}}J_{\text{res}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Penalty}}\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>mAP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mtext>perf</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Performance</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>stab</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mtext>stab</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Stability</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mtext>conv</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Convergence</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>pen</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mtext>res</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Penalty</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}\left(\underbrace{w_{\text{mAP}}J_{\text{perf}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Performance}}+\underbrace{w_{\text{stab}}J_{\text{stab}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Stability}}+\underbrace{w_{\text{conv}}J_{\text{conv}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Convergence}}-\underbrace{w_{\text{pen}}J_{\text{res}}^{(t+1)}}_{\text{Penalty}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Maximizing this objective leads the agent toward a sequence of <em id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Pareto optimal</em> training strategies <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{C_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{C_{t}\}_{t=0}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, where no single objective can be improved without degrading another. Different weight settings <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w_{\text{mAP}},w_{\text{stab}},w_{\text{conv}},w_{\text{pen}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>mAP</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>stab</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>pen</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w_{\text{mAP}},w_{\text{stab}},w_{\text{conv}},w_{\text{pen}})</annotation></semantics></math> enable the agent to navigate the <em id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Pareto front</em>, tailoring trade-offs to context-specific requirements such as accuracy or efficiency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.2 </span>Informational Perspective: Efficient Knowledge Acquisition and Representation Learning</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although the reward function of MAT-Agent is not rigorously constructed based on core information-theoretic formulas (e.g., optimizing mutual information or entropy expressions directly), its individual components exhibit clear intuitive alignment with fundamental principles in information theory regarding efficient information processing, effective learning, and knowledge representation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accuracy and Improvement Term (<math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{w_{\text{mAP}}f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})}_{\text{accuracy-weighted reward}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">mAP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">mAP</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">accuracy-weighted reward</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{w_{\text{mAP}}f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})}_{\text{accuracy-weighted reward}}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">This term aims to improve the consistency between the predicted labels <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> (parameterized by <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and the ground-truth labels <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>. From an information-theoretic perspective, this aligns with the goal of maximizing the <span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">mutual information</span> <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;\hat{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;\hat{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> between the two. Mutual information quantifies how much information about one random variable (e.g., the true label <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>) can be obtained by observing another (e.g., the predicted label <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;\hat{Y})=\underbrace{H(Y)}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Prior entropy of true label }Y\\
\text{Reflects intrinsic uncertainty/information in }Y\end{subarray}}-\underbrace{H(Y|\hat{Y})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Conditional entropy (posterior uncertainty)}\\
\text{Reflects remaining uncertainty in }Y\text{ after observing }\hat{Y}\end{subarray}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>Prior entropy of true label </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>Reflects intrinsic uncertainty/information in </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>Conditional entropy (posterior uncertainty)</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mtext>Reflects remaining uncertainty in </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> after observing </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;\hat{Y})=\underbrace{H(Y)}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Prior entropy of true label }Y\\
\text{Reflects intrinsic uncertainty/information in }Y\end{subarray}}-\underbrace{H(Y|\hat{Y})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{Conditional entropy (posterior uncertainty)}\\
\text{Reflects remaining uncertainty in }Y\text{ after observing }\hat{Y}\end{subarray}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stability Contribution (<math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{w_{\text{stab}}\text{Stability}_{t}}_{\text{stability-weighted reward}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">stab</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Stability</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">stability-weighted reward</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{w_{\text{stab}}\text{Stability}_{t}}_{\text{stability-weighted reward}}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">This term penalizes instability during training (e.g., excessive loss fluctuations), encouraging smoother learning curves. From the lens of information transmission, the training process—especially gradient computation and parameter updates—can be viewed as a channel conveying signals about how to adjust parameters to improve the model. Instability (e.g., gradient noise or direction fluctuations) acts as noise in this signal channel:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta_{\text{update}}\approx f(\underbrace{\mathcal{S}_{\text{opt}}}_{\text{desired optimization signal}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{N}_{\text{train}}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{noise from sampling, stochastic optimization,}\\
\text{and gradient estimation errors}\end{subarray}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>update</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>desired optimization signal</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mtext>noise from sampling, stochastic optimization,</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>and gradient estimation errors</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta_{\text{update}}\approx f(\underbrace{\mathcal{S}_{\text{opt}}}_{\text{desired optimization signal}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{N}_{\text{train}}}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{noise from sampling, stochastic optimization,}\\
\text{and gradient estimation errors}\end{subarray}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Convergence Speed Contribution (<math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{w_{\text{conv}}\text{Convergence}_{t}}_{\text{convergence-weighted reward}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">conv</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Convergence</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">convergence-weighted reward</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{w_{\text{conv}}\text{Convergence}_{t}}_{\text{convergence-weighted reward}}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">The term <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Convergence}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Convergence</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Convergence}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> rewards strategies that more quickly reach target performance or lower loss, which can be interpreted as reducing residual uncertainty or encoding redundancy in the model. This resonates with the ideas of <span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">coding efficiency</span> and <span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">information compression</span> from algorithmic information theory or the MDL principle, and aligns with machine learning goals of sample/computational efficiency. If we view learning as a search over parameter space <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> for the optimal <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, with bounded training budget <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the intuitive training efficiency can be expressed as:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Efficiency}\propto\frac{\Delta P(\theta(t))}{\Delta(\text{Resource Consumption})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Efficiency</mtext><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Resource Consumption</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Efficiency}\propto\frac{\Delta P(\theta(t))}{\Delta(\text{Resource Consumption})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overall Reasonableness of the Reward Design:</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">Based on the above perspectives, the composite reward function <math id="A2.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> in MAT-Agent reflects several levels of rationality:</p>
<ul id="A2.I3.i4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-dimensional assessment and balance:</span> It goes beyond a single objective by incorporating accuracy (<math id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\text{mAP}}f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>mAP</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>mAP</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\text{mAP}}f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>), stability (<math id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\text{stab}}\text{Stability}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>stab</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Stability</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\text{stab}}\text{Stability}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>), convergence speed (<math id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\text{conv}}\text{Convergence}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Convergence</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\text{conv}}\text{Convergence}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>), and resource/risk cost (<math id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-w_{\text{pen}}\text{Penalty}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>pen</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Penalty</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-w_{\text{pen}}\text{Penalty}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) to guide the agent towards balanced learning behaviors, avoiding overfitting to any single metric.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive reward dynamics:</span> Terms like <math id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>mAP</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\Delta\text{mAP}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> dynamically adjust the incentive strength based on the current training phase.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Practical applicability:</span> The penalty term <math id="A2.I3.i4.I0.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\text{pen}}\text{Penalty}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext>pen</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Penalty</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\text{pen}}\text{Penalty}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures the agent avoids strategies that are inefficient, computationally expensive, or infeasible in real-world deployment.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
